<p>See the full <a href="/strata/alternatives">Strata alternatives</a> comparison for more detail.</p>

<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

<h3>Does Strata publish pricing?</h3>
<p>No. Strata pricing is custom-quoted and is not listed as public monthly or annual plans.</p>

<h3>Is Strata priced per user?</h3>
<p>Seat count is usually one pricing factor, but enterprise media management contracts can also depend on modules, offices, markets, integrations, and transaction volume.</p>

<h3>Is Strata only for TV buying?</h3>
<p>No. Strata has deep roots in traditional media buying, but its current positioning covers cross-media campaign management, digital workflows, financial operations, and reporting.</p>

<h3>What should buyers ask before signing?</h3>
<p>Ask which modules are included, how implementation is scoped, whether finance integrations are extra, how user seats are counted, and what support is included after go-live.</p>

<h3>How does Strata compare with Mediaocean on cost?</h3>
<p>Both are enterprise systems with custom pricing. The better benchmark is not list price, but the modules needed, integration burden, agency workflow fit, and finance requirements.</p>

<h2>Sources & Methodology</h2>

